`AddHDKey()` only validates the private scalar with `key.key.IsValid()`. 

The current code can throw `std::out_of_range` in production at `WalletDescriptor w_desc(std::move(descs.at(0)), ...);` if a non-RPC provides a structurally malformed CExtKey whose scalar remains valid. For example:

```c++
    CExtKey key;
    key.SetSeed(GenerateRandomKey());
    key.nChild = 1;

    auto result = interface->addHDKey(key)
```

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
